const TOWN_NOTES={guild_charter:{title:'The Gilded Paw Charter',text:'Port Felin began as a river toll town. The cat guilds eventually bought a civic charter that lets the guild hall police the roads, settle trade disputes and post public contracts.'},eastroad:{title:'Eastroad and the Redtails',text:'The Stone Bridge is the old boundary of Port Felin. Beyond it, the Eastroad climbs toward Mosswood and the Old Quarry, where Redtail foxes have tried to collect their own illegal tolls.'},river_trade:{title:'The Silver River',text:'The Silver River feeds Port Felin as much as any road. Dace are common near the north bank and old quay, while reeds from the shallows are prized by tailors and basket makers.'},market_trade:{title:'Mercato Trade',text:'Mercato prices rise when caravans stop reaching town. Iron, medicinal herbs and clean pelts usually fetch the steadiest crowns; common provisions are cheap because the river keeps Port Felin supplied.'},apothecary:{title:'Saffron’s Red Tonic',text:'Saffron refuses to reveal the full recipe, but admits the familiar field version starts with rosemary and black grapes. The guild treats the tonic as road medicine, not a luxury.'},exchange:{title:'The Felin Exchange',text:'The Exchange grew from guild strongboxes into Port Felin’s public bank. Items and crowns stored in its vault persist safely between expeditions, and banked crowns are not part of the purse lost when an adventurer is carried home after defeat.'},hermetic_arts:{title:'The Hermetic Arts',text:'Port Felin apothecaries treat aethercraft as disciplined natural philosophy: glass, salts, metal and measured breath focus a short-lived current. Heavy armor interferes with delicate casting, while trained scholars conserve Focus and recover it quickly.'},bellflower_vale:{title:'Bellflower Vale',text:'Bellflower Vale lies beyond the Eastroad charter stones. Cat vintners and shepherds once paid Port Felin for patrols, but the Sable Company now occupies the old aqueduct and demands its own tolls with pikes and smoke-powder guns.'},masterworks:{title:'Guild Masterworks',text:'Port Felin artisans call an item masterwork only after its materials have been refined separately: charcoal for clean heat, quarry steel for strength, foxhide lining for flex, Bellflower oil for sealing, and aetherglass for precise hermetic focusing. The Gilded Paw records each maker’s mark.'},guild_standing:{title:'Guild Standing',text:'The Gilded Paw records service as renown. Permanent commissions and repeatable contracts both count. Higher rank improves contract pay, Mercato terms and wayshrine priority, while Bellflower keeps a separate local record of cats who defend the vale.'},festival_customs:{title:'The Seven-Day Festival Cycle',text:'Port Felin’s civic week is practical rather than sacred: Market Day brings caravans, Guild Day musters patrols, River Day blesses the fishery, and Vale Day draws Bellflower growers into town. The bellkeeper records cats who serve through the whole cycle.'}};
TOWN_NOTES.weatherwise_wanderer={title:'Fieldcraft in Three Weathers',text:'Port Felin roadwardens measure a good patrol by what it brings home: fish in the river rain, fresh herbs in low mist, and a safe return after crossing hostile ground in gusting wind. Oilskin field coats are stitched to keep arrows steady when the weather turns.'};
